{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>וַיִּקָּדֵשׁ בָּם</b> — that Moses and Aaron died on account of them: when the Holy One, blessed be He, executes judgment upon His consecrated ones, He is feared and sanctified among the creatures, as it is said: \"בִּקְרֹבַי אֶקָּדֵשׁ\" (Leviticus 10:3), and likewise it says: \"נוֹרָא אֱלֹהִים מִמִּקְדָּשֶׁיךָ\" (Psalms 68:36). This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 20:13). Ibn Ezra also explained it this way (Ibn Ezra on Numbers 20:13). But it does not seem correct in my eyes, for Moses and Aaron had not yet died, and it was not publicized to the creatures that they would die on account of this sin, so that the Holy One, blessed be He, would thereby be feared — as was the case with Nadab and Abihu and with the smiting of Uzzah (2 Samuel 6:8). Moreover, the verse says: \"אֲשֶׁר רָבוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת ה׳ וַיִּקָּדֵשׁ בָּם\" — that through the strife He was sanctified, in the language of \"בִּקְרֹבַי אֶקָּדֵשׁ\" — and it would have been fitting for their words that it say \"וַיִּכָּבֵד עַל פְּנֵיהֶם\" (and He was heavy upon their faces). And what seems correct in my eyes is that the matter of the first rock was before the eyes of the elders of Israel alone, as is explicitly stated there (Exodus 17:6–7), whereas concerning this one He said: \"וַיַּקְהִילוּ מֹשֶׁה וְאַהֲרֹן אֶת הַקָּהָל\" etc. Therefore the verse states that these waters of Meribah, in which the decree was decreed upon Moses and Aaron — they are those waters of Meribah in which the children of Israel strove with HaShem, and He was sanctified through them before the eyes of them all, in the manner written: \"וְקִבַּצְתִּי אֹתָם מֵאַרְצוֹת אֹיְבֵיהֶם וְנִקְדַּשְׁתִּי בָם לְעֵינֵי הַגּוֹיִם רַבִּים\" (Ezekiel 39:27). And know that in the first instance they had a quarrel with Moses, as it says: \"וַיָּרֶב הָעָם עִם מֹשֶׁה\" (Exodus 17:2), and likewise it says: \"עוֹד מְעַט וּסְקָלֻנִי\" (ibid. v. 4), and they were testing HaShem: \"הֲיֵשׁ ה׳ בְּקִרְבֵּנוּ\" (ibid. v. 7). But here they strove toward above, and there was no testing here; therefore he said that these waters of Meribah, in which this decree was decreed upon them — they are the waters of Meribah in which the children of Israel strove with HaShem, and He was sanctified through them before their eyes, and not the first ones in which they tested HaShem, and He was not sanctified except before the eyes of the elders of Israel. And because the matter of the rock occurred twice, it was necessary to explain upon which of them the righteous ones were punished."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The parenthetical reference '(ו׳ ח׳)' after Uzzah appears to cite 2 Samuel 6:8 (the smiting of Uzzah); resolved accordingly."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:07:17.550043146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}